# shir_nodes/type_assert.node — TypeAssert: a dynamic type assertion.
#
# GENERIC (any frontend with runtime type checks: Go `x.(T)` and its
# comma-ok form, Zig @as-style checked casts, Java `instanceof`-narrowed
# reads). The IR is dynamically typed, so the assertion is a CHECKED
# PASSTHROUGH: the value flows through unchanged; `kind` names the
# expected dynamic kind so backends that CAN check may validate.
#
# kind vocabulary = the sh2.typeOf strings already pinned by the type-
# switch lowering: "string" | "int" | "float" | "bool" | "array".
# The comma-ok boolean is NOT part of this node: a frontend emits the
# comparison `typeof(x) == kind` itself (same vocabulary), keeping the
# node single-responsibility.

node TypeAssert
tag "TypeAssert"
kind expr
# storage_class str_bounded
field expr: expr
field kind: string
